<title>NETHERLANDS: NBM-Amstel takes charge for unit closure.</title>
<headline>NBM-Amstel takes charge for unit closure.</headline>
<dateline>THE HAGUE 1997-04-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dutch builder NBM-Amstelland NV said on Thursday it had booked a net extraordinary charge of 1.7 million guilders arising from the closure of its loss-making soil decontamination unit in Schiedam near Rotterdam.</p>
<p>It said the decontamination installation had made a loss for the third consecutive year.</p>
<p>&quot;Because the outlook on the environmental market is still less than rosy, the installation was closed at the end of the year under review,&quot; NBM said.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
</text>
